    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p67-q3-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": {
          "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
          "version": 1,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "p67-q3-a-instruction",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 2,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Estimate the percentage of participants who regularly cycle to school.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$20\\%$.\n\nCombine the gold-card and blue-card cases that produce a True response.",
          "worked": "Let $C$ be the event that a participant regularly cycles to school, $T$ the event of a True response, and $p=P(C)$. A True response occurs for a cyclist drawing gold or a non-cyclist drawing blue.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\widehat{P}(T)&=\\frac{585}{900}\\\\\\widehat{P}(T)&=\\frac{13}{20}\\end{align*}$$\n\n$$\\begin{align*}P(T)&=\\frac14p+\\frac34(1-p)\\\\P(T)&=\\frac34-\\frac12p\\end{align*}$$\n\nUsing the observed proportion to estimate $P(T)$,\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{13}{20}&=\\frac34-\\frac12p\\\\\\frac12p&=\\frac1{10}\\\\p&=\\frac15\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe estimated percentage is $20\\%$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 106
      },
      {
        "id": "p67-q3-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": {
          "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
          "version": 1,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "p67-q3-b-instruction",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 2,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "For a participant who answered ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "True",
                  "marks": [
                    "italic"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": ", what is the probability that they do in fact regularly cycle to school?",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac1{13}$.\n\nDivide the probability of cycling and responding True by the total probability of responding True.",
          "worked": "Let $C$ denote regularly cycling to school and $T$ a True response. From part (a), use $P(C)=\\frac15$ and $P(T)=\\frac{13}{20}$. A cyclist responds True only when drawing the gold card.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}P(C\\cap T)&=\\frac15\\times\\frac14\\\\P(C\\cap T)&=\\frac1{20}\\end{align*}$$\n\n$$\\begin{align*}P(C\\mid T)&=\\frac{P(C\\cap T)}{P(T)}\\\\P(C\\mid T)&=\\frac{\\frac1{20}}{\\frac{13}{20}}\\\\P(C\\mid T)&=\\frac1{13}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 78
      }
    ]
